  "design": "Weapon and armor use independently equipped levels. Common +1, +3 and +5 progress from simple bindings to engraving. Epic +1–5 shares the common +5 silhouette. Epic +6 adds a physical collar or layered lappet; +9 adds its crowning work. Plate, oakleaf mantle and celestial stole have distinct back and side trains. The high-tier sword has a gilded crimson full blade fitted between the existing hilt and tip; the staff has its own crystal crown; the bow adds a second finial only where the original lower nock is exposed. A separate cloth insignia on the shoulder records chapter rank at hero Lv4 and Lv8.",
  "derivation": "Use the listed boundaries on each original; linearly remap alpha 12..248 to 0..255. Trim the alpha-64 box plus a 2-pixel border and fit within 122 x 122 using Lanczos. Center each piece in one 128-pixel atlas cell, armor then weapons.",
